","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms/Trees/RootedTree/eulerTour":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/Trees\/RootedTree\/eulerTour","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/trees\/rootedtree\/eulertour","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The closed walk from the root that goes down each child edge, in "},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and back up it after that subtree: 2n − 1 vertices, each edge position twice (NetworkX"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"dfs_labeled_edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", forward then reverse). The trivial walk for one vertex. O(n)."}],"title":"eulerTour","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"eulerTour"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4WalkV","text":"Walk"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic"}}}